From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 09:53:42 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] dcomp: run an InteractionTracker's custom animations and
 inertia.

Word scrolls its document with the mouse wheel by handing the canvas's
tracker a Vector3 key frame animation, one key frame at the end and 267ms
long, through TryUpdatePositionWithAnimation.  That was a stub that left the
position where it was, so the wheel moved the scroll bar and nothing else.

The tracker is now the state machine Windows documents: idle, a custom
animation, inertia, and interacting, which only input brings about and so
cannot be reached yet.  Each request takes the next request id before
anything else is looked at, is ignored while input moves the tracker, and
tells the owner of the state it enters, with the id of the request that
took it there; values that change on a frame are reported with it too.

- TryUpdatePositionWithAnimation and TryUpdateScaleWithAnimation run the
  animation as a "motion": an animation run on a value of the tracker's own
  rather than started on a property, checked and copied as a started one is
  and counted in the batches.  The tracker reads it each frame and keeps it
  within its bounds, as the documentation says custom animations always are;
  scale is animated about the given center point.  When every one of its
  animations has ended it is idle again, for the request that started it.
- TryUpdatePosition, TryUpdatePositionBy and TryUpdateScale end whatever
  moves it, unless told that an animation of scale may go on.
- The velocity requests set it coasting: each axis loses the same fraction
  of its velocity every second, the decay rate, 0.95 unless set, and comes to
  rest where that ends, or where the first inertia modifier whose condition
  holds says, within bounds.  InertiaStateEntered says where it would have
  rested, where it will, and how fast it went.  Center point modifiers move
  the point scale inertia keeps in place.  Motion modifiers are not run.
- The modifiers a VisualInteractionSource is configured with are kept, for
  the input that would use them.

What Windows answers there and then was measured on a Windows 11 desktop
(build 29671), in tools/trackerprobe: an animation of the wrong type, a Vector2 one or a scalar
expression for position, fails with E_INVALIDARG after taking a request id,
without handing it back; a clamping or update option out of range fails
after handing its id back; StartAnimation takes a tracker's bounds but not
its position, scale, resting places or velocities.  That session was locked,
so its compositor drew no frames and what happens over time could not be
measured there; that part follows the documentation, and its tests skip
where no frames come.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit c6024d31f1cfa8e18b8d808db4418d472d54b73c)

